# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build output
#
# Two applications live in this tree now, each with its own build directory:
# the QML app (root CMakeLists.txt) and the Widgets client (cpp/CMakeLists.txt).
# Both are per-machine -- Windows builds with the ROS distro's own CMake, and a
# tree made by a different CMake or generator cannot be reused.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
build/
build-*/
out/
CMakeCache.txt
CMakeFiles/
cmake_install.cmake
CTestTestfile.cmake
Testing/
compile_commands.json
*.o
*.a
*.so
*.so.*
*.dylib
*.dll
*.exe

# Qt generated (AUTOMOC / AUTOUIC / AUTORCC)
#
# `ui_*.h` is why subapp_3d_verification/views/widgets/UI3d_measurement.h is
# named WITHOUT the prefix: it is committed uic output, and the prefixed name
# would be both ignored here and regenerated by AUTOUIC.
*_autogen/
moc_*.cpp
moc_*.h
qrc_*.cpp
ui_*.h
*.qm
.qmake.stash

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ROS 2 / colcon
#
# ros/moil_interfaces/ is SOURCE and is tracked. Only what colcon writes beside
# it -- ros/install/, ros/log/, ros/build/ -- is ignored.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
install/
log/
devel/
.catkin_tools/
COLCON_IGNORE
AMENT_IGNORE
# ...except the server's, which is SOURCE rather than a stray marker in a build
# tree. Server/*/common/ is a plain CMake library with a CMakeLists.txt and no
# package.xml, deliberately not a ROS package; the marker is what stops a
# `colcon build` run from the server folder trying to build it as one. Ignored,
# it would be missing from every fresh clone -- which is exactly the machine that
# would hit it.
!Server/*/common/COLCON_IGNORE

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Runtime output written by the apps (patterns, captures, 3D results)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
image_cali/

# Sample calibration images (~31 MB of PNGs).
# Remove this line if you DO want the sample dataset in the repo.
image_example/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Packaging artifacts
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.7z
*.tar.gz
*.tar.xz
*.deb
*.AppImage
Output/
dist/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editors / IDE
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
*.user
*.swp
*~
.cache/
.ccls-cache/
.clangd/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OS / filesystem junk
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Windows "mark of the web" alternate data streams, created when files are
# copied from Windows into WSL.
*Zone.Identifier
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini
.DS_Store

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Claude Code
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.claude/

# ANCHORED ON PURPOSE, and this is load-bearing now that doc/ has arrived.
#
# `/docs/` is the QML app's notes directory, of which only RUNNING.md,
# MINIPC_ROS_CONNECT.md and BACKEND_INTEGRATION.md are tracked (force-added).
# Unanchored, `docs/` would ALSO match doc/moilcalib_documentation/docs/ -- the
# whole v2.0 page tree -- and git would drop it from every commit without
# saying a word.
/docs/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Superseded QML-app scaffolding
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
mvc_controller/
mvc_model/
mvc_view/

aqtinstall.log

# Generated by tools/dummy_image.py; the tracked copy lives at assets/sample_shot.png
tools/sample_shot.png

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Docker client: per-site settings and the volumes it writes into
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
docker/.env
docker/data/
docker/urlqueue/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Server: per-machine dependency overrides and scratch output.
#
# deps.local.bat is where MOIL_WS_BASE is set per checkout -- OLD and this tree
# share a machine, and moil_env.bat's default (%SystemDrive%\moil_ws) is shared
# between them. Yours alone; never committed.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
Server/*/deps.local.bat
Server/*/server_env.bat
# _st.bat dumps /system/status here.
Server/*/st.txt

# Written by the pattern panels' Export; the fixed Documents folder is code-side.
pattern_json/
